{"description":"Structured logs, metrics and health for the coordinator, bound to the tailnet interface only.\n\nOne metric is not optional and is the reason this item sits in the MVP rather than a later phase: the **direct-versus-relay ratio**. The hybrid topology in walkie/adr:001-transport-topology will keep working while silently relaying everything if direct paths never form, which would make the central architectural decision unobservable in production. The metric is the mitigation for the one substantive disagreement recorded in this project's planning.\n\nThe ratio has no traffic to measure until phase 2 delivers the direct data plane, so the MVP delivers the instrument and the phase-2 work supplies the readings.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. Logs are structured JSON with a consistent severity scheme, and carry no message content or key material.\n2. Metrics cover: connected devices, queue depth per recipient, queue evictions by TTL and by size cap, messages per second, authentication refusals, and reconnect rate.\n3. The direct-versus-relay counter exists and is exported from the MVP onward, even while it necessarily reads zero direct paths.\n4. A health endpoint reports coordinator and store readiness separately.\n5. Metrics and health bind to the tailnet interface only, verified by test.\n6. No metric label carries a device identity in a form that turns the metrics endpoint into a presence side channel."}